      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-1,3],$ find $\\text{Var}[X].$",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-1$ and $b=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(3-(-1))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{16}{12}=\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$",
